{
  "Name": "Hallows_Eve_Old_Jack",
  "$Comment": [
    "Old Jack's conversation, everything he says while Hallow's Eve runs, wherever his placement",
    "stands him (the Forgotten Temple, unless a server owner moves him). He contracts everything he",
    "says: I'm, it's, don't.",
    "",
    "HOW A SCREEN IS PICKED. Start is walked in a fixed order: First (top to bottom), then a quest",
    "that is READY to hand in, then one he can OFFER, then one that is ACTIVE, then Then, then",
    "Fallback.",
    "",
    "First holds four beats. The welcome comes first, for a player carrying Lanterns in the Temple",
    "(the quest every player gets while the event runs): its answer marks him greeted and opens his",
    "quest list on that quest, where the player hands it in and collects it, and collecting it plays",
    "this conversation again. Then the greeting, for anyone who came without that quest, shown until",
    "its answer spends it. Then Pumpkin Patch's offer, once (OnceId meet_patch_offer), for a player",
    "who has handed the intro in and not taken Pumpkin Patch, so the questline opens straight after",
    "the welcome is collected. Then the board line, once a day (Once with Period Daily, turning over",
    "at midnight UTC) and skipped while the player has something to hand in. Its Actions pay a little",
    "favor with Old Jack (the Reputation reward; Amount is how much) when the player finishes the",
    "line, whichever answer they pick, goodnight and trick-or-treat included; Escape pays nothing.",
    "",
    "Quests holds one row per quest: the intro, the questline, then the dailies, so the questline",
    "wins a tie with a daily. The intro's row brings the welcome back for a player who gave that",
    "quest up or whose quest log was full when it tried to arm: that answer takes it and opens his",
    "quest list on it. While a quest is being worked on, its Active screen says what to do and where,",
    "one screen per kind of work: active_pumpkins (Pumpkin Patch, Pumpkin Rounds), active_bombs",
    "(Lantern Work), active_night (Ghouls on the Steps, Ectoplasm Run, Restless Souls, and The Hollow",
    "Lantern, whose skeletons, Ectoplasm and pumpkin all come from the night) and active_stone (Cursed",
    "Stone, Geodes for Jack). The Rider is offered on rider_offer beside his errands, and its Active",
    "screen is his rider line, horseman. Both say the Gravekeeper's gate wants a Grave Candle and that",
    "Jack sells them, since The Rider's first step is buying one, and horseman carries the stall one",
    "press away; Fire for the Lantern, the hard ride for the Horseman's Ember,",
    "has ember_offer and active_ember, which send the player to the Gravekeeper for the hard ride and",
    "say its gate wants a Burning Grave Candle, sold at the stall once Jack counts them a Regular. An",
    "offer's answer takes its quest and goes straight to that screen, so the player hears what to do",
    "and where the moment they take it. Pumpkin Patch, Fire for the Lantern (ember_ready) and the",
    "lantern quest have hand-in lines of their own; the rest share",
    "ready_generic, which opens his quest list for the hand-in. The three dailies share daily_offer,",
    "one answer each, shown while that daily is free to take. Then shows the lit-lantern line while",
    "this year's lantern burns (the lantern quest reads ON_COOLDOWN until it comes back next year).",
    "",
    "THE MENU. The steady screens carry jack_menu, the one menu: What needs doing?, his quest list,",
    "where the jobs his daily board and his errands board (Hallows_Eve_Daily, Hallows_Eve_Errands) post",
    "list beside his quests, since both boards name him in Hosts, then the stall, What are the",
    "sweets for? (what Hallow Sweets buy and how they are earned, with the stall one press away),",
    "How do we stand? (the Reputation page, shown once the player has any favor with him), the Almanac",
    "(only while the Almanac is switched on), the rider (where to find the Headless Horseman and how",
    "to beat him; once the player has beaten him, horseman_beaten instead, read off the Almanac's",
    "Horseman_Down tally as the ziggfreedcommon:counter key hallows_eve/horseman_down, so with the",
    "Almanac or the stat store switched off the first line stays), who he is, the Harvest Moon line",
    "(only while Harvest Moon runs) and goodnight. A screen that asks something of the player carries",
    "jack_back instead: back to the menu, or goodnight. Chrome words the exit row the page adds to a",
    "screen with no goodnight of its own. The trick-or-treat line is not here: the DialogueExtensions file",
    "Hallows_Eve_Trick_Or_Treat adds it to every conversation, this one included.",
    "",
    "No line asks which world the player is in, so the welcome, the greeting and Pumpkin Patch's offer",
    "play wherever he stands: the conversation is reached only through him (his placement's Interact),",
    "and Season keeps him standing only while the event runs. The greeting's memory carries no Where,",
    "so it is kept once per player, the same in every world, and its ResetWithQuest files it under his",
    "meet quest (Lanterns in the Temple): it is forgotten whenever that quest is reset, so a player who",
    "starts the questline over hears his first words again. It can be written before that quest starts."
  ],
